 "description": "What is the probability of an event A given that event B has occurred? We call this conditional probability, and it is governed by the formula that P(A|B) which reads \"probability of A given B\" is equal to the P(A intersect B)/P(B). We look at an example involving the probability of being an alcoholic given that one is a man. \n\nConditional Probability Formula: P(A|B) = P(A and B)/P(B) \n\n►FULL DISC",
